WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.030
Here's how to change what a button does,

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.370
quiet a drifting stick, and make a trigger reach full sooner.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.530
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:13.135
Open your controller's page, then its Mappings tab.

5
00:00:13.645 --> 00:00:16.935
Each row is one output the game sees, and A comes first.

6
00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:20.129
To make your pad's B button drive A,

7
00:00:20.169 --> 00:00:24.049
click the A row, open its Source list, and pick B.

8
00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:25.399
It takes effect at once.

9
00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.246
Do the same on the B row, and pick A.

10
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:31.776
The swap is done, and there is no save step.

11
00:00:33.051 --> 00:00:35.721
With the pad in hand, the record button is quicker.

12
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:38.161
Click it, then press the button you want.

13
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:47.242
On the Sticks tab, raise Deadzone X and Y a little, to ignore a drifting stick.

14
00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:50.722
The circle beside them shows the stick before and after.

15
00:00:52.066 --> 00:00:55.356
On the Triggers tab, pull the right end of Range in,

16
00:00:55.566 --> 00:00:58.016
and the trigger reads full before it bottoms out.

17
00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:02.618
Each change works at once, and PadForge saves it for you.

18
00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:05.098
Find more guides at padforge.org.
